me><etal/></person-group><article-title>The <inline-formula><mml:math id="M9"><mml:mrow><mml:msup><mml:mrow><mml:mtext>Pro</mml:mtext></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mn>12</mml:mn></mml:mrow></mml:msup><mml:mo>&#x02192;</mml:mo><mml:mtext>Ala</mml:mtext></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> substitution in PPAR-<inline-formula><mml:math id="M10"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b3;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>  is associated with resistance to development of diabetes in the general population: possible involvement in impairment of insulin secretion in individuals with type 2 diabetes</article-title><source><italic>Diabetes</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>50</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>891</fpage><lpage>894</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11289058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Memisoglu</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>FB</given-names></name><name><surname>Hankinson</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prospective study of the association between the proline to alanine codon 12 polymorphism in the <italic>PPAR</italic><inline-formula><mml:math id="M11"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003b3;</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> gene and type 2 diabetes</article-title><source><italic>Diabetes Care</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>2915</fpage><lpage>2917</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14514601</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Florez</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Jablonski</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sun</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of the type 2 diabetes-associate